Linux is a free and open-source operating system based on the Unix operating system. It is widely used for servers, desktops, cloud computing, embedded systems, and Android devices. Linux is known for its security, stability, speed, and flexibility.
Features of Linux
Open source and free
Multi-user operating system
Multitasking support
Secure and reliable
Portable (runs on many hardware platforms)
Supports networking
Powerful command-line interface
Common Linux Distributions
Ubuntu
Fedora
Debian
Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL)
CentOS
Linux Mint
Kali Linux



pwd
Shows the current directory.
ls
Lists files and folders.
ls -l
Shows detailed file information.
ls -a
Shows all files, including hidden files.
cd Documents
Moves to the Documents folder.
cd.
Moves to the parent directory.
mkdir Test
Creates a folder named Test.
touch file.txt
Creates an empty file named file.txt.
cat file.txt
Displays the contents of file.txt.
echo "Hello Linux"
Prints Hello Linux on the terminal.
echo "Hello Linux" > file.txt
Writes text into file.txt.
cp file.txt copy.txt
cd ..
